1: # Plan 6: prepared mask execution
2: 
3: Draft for independent admission/preflight and storage/undo reviews. Mesh MASK
4: already fits the prepared scalar path; grids currently reject `writesMask`.
5: This slice admits the existing built-in mask storage policy without enabling
6: general attribute mirrors, face kernels, layer writes or host-stage commands.
7: 
8: ## Implementation
9: 
10: 1. Keep every existing capability restriction except the grid writesMask blanket
11:    rejection. Before admitting a mask-writing command, require an existing named
12:    mask channel (if any) to be one FLOAT component in the vertex domain. Do not create it
13:    during supports queries, validateOnly or rejected program preflight.
14: 2. Ensure the mask channel inside execStage for every accepted nonempty mask
15:    stage, before capture. `ensureMaskChannel()` is an idempotent lookup. Its old
16:    first-dab-only condition fails after an earlier zero/missed dab or after a
17:    preceding non-mask dab consumed first-of-step state. Retain normal raw behavior
18:    except this correctness fix. Rejected/zero/empty dabs must not create storage.
19: 3. Use the existing GridCapturePolicy mask snapshots, moved-vertex union and
20:    stroke-end grid-block capture/flush. Prepared scalar evaluation and maximum
21:    command-radius selection already occur before this stage. Programs retain
22:    full preflight and working-state restoration. No native API or schema change.
23: 4. Preserve existing undo semantics: undo restores mask values and store blocks;
24:    a lazily created neutral mask channel may remain, as in the current raw path.
25:    Test channel presence independently of mask data and never claim byte-identical
26:    whole-store serialization across first-ever channel creation.
27: 
28: ## Acceptance
29: 
30: - Multi-leaf mesh/grid MASK and DRAW+MASK prepared versus independent raw
31:   reference; inherited/explicit-empty strength stacks, varying pressure/tilt,
32:   larger growing secondary radius, inversion, zero and absent input.
33: - Exact mask, geometry and preexisting store-block undo/redo; new channel created
34:   only after accepted region hit. Zero/miss first dab then real hit; non-mask first
35:   dab then mask. Later invalid command leaves channel inventory, masks, positions,
36:   undo state, counters and first-dab state unchanged before any creation.
37: - Reject malformed existing mask channel shape/domain before capture/publication.
38:   Do not relax other attribute/mirror/face/layer/host restrictions.
39: - Dispatcher native/Python builds; applicable 17-suite regression, actual DLL
40:   input batches, safe headed Alt-mask mesh/grid Python/batch queued/delayed matrix.
41:   Require prepared calls and score actual mask values (not geometry movement).
42:   Stage matching package and record provenance smoke plus completion evidence.
